WHAT YOU MAY DO WITH THIS SUBTREE

You are granted permission, at no cost and without needing to ask us, to:

  - read, study and review every file here;
  - run it, including compiling and executing the reference implementation in
    src/, on any machine you control, for any purpose including commercial
    evaluation;
  - reproduce its outputs and report what you measured, whether or not what you
    measured agrees with what we published;
  - quote and cite it, in academic work, in a review, or in an argument that we
    are wrong.

Those are the uses this artifact exists for. Nothing here is intended to stop a
referee, a customer or a competitor from checking our claims.

WHAT IS NOT GRANTED

Redistribution. You may not publish, mirror, repackage or distribute this
subtree, or a modified version of it, to third parties.

WHY THIS IS NARROWER THAN THE REST OF THE TREE

Everything else in this download is Apache-2.0, which permits redistribution.
This subtree is not, and it is a deliberate choice rather than an oversight or
a leftover.

A licence grant is one-way. Apache-2.0 text that we publish today cannot be
withdrawn from the copies already made, so granting redistribution before the
terms are settled is a decision that can never be revisited. Reserving it can:
if you need redistribution rights, ask, and we can grant them. We cannot
un-grant them.

The paper itself is not yet placed, and where it lands may carry its own terms
for the text, the figures and the bibliography. Publishing those under an
irrevocable licence in advance of that is the kind of thing that is discovered
later and cannot be fixed.

None of this restricts the use that matters. If your goal is to check whether
our numbers are real, this licence grants you everything you need and asks
nothing of you.

If you want terms this does not give you, write to us and we will settle it.
